{\b\ulw Leftover Debugging Functions}\par
{\b 1)} {\ulw The Debug Room - Tileset Viewer (Map ID: 0E)}\par
   One of two dev rooms remaining in the game.\par
   This map simply lays out all 16x16 tiles in the maps tileset in a 16x12 grid pattern.\par
   The layer 2 tiles will be laid out in the same grid pattern and 50% transparent. It also slowly scrolls southward.\par
   The map is set to display the Town Exterior (Index 00) tileset, however if you edit the header others can be viewed.\par
   Navigation is difficult to impossible without disabling collision.\par
   Additionally this map doesn't have any triggers defined, so walking on a trigger tile will end up using a map trigger from Potos Village Outskirts (Map ID: 10) instead.\par
   No doors exist that lead to this map, a door must be hacked to gain access.\par
\par
{\b 2)} {\ulw The Debug Room - Developer Room (Map ID: 0F)}\par
   One of two dev rooms remaining in the game and the most well known of the two.\par
   The map is of maximum size, is solid black, and contains 9 NPCs, 8 near the entry point and one off-screen to the right.\par
   The 8 nearby NPCs are assigned Debug Events 400-405 and Debug Events 8E-8F. The off-screen Snowman NPC is assigned default Event 0.\par
   The functions of all debug events have been removed and are now just stubs, except for Debug Event 400 (assigned to the King NPC).\par
   In Seiken Densetsu 2 Debug Event 400 is a stub just like the rest of them, however during localization the intro sequence was moved to Bank 0A and assigned the ID of 400.\par
   As a result, the only remaining function of this room is to replay the intro sequence, and only because of a side effect of localization.\par
   The Purim & Popoie NPCs are set to not appear if they are in your party and they use Debug Events 8E-8F instead of in the 400 range.\par
   The likely function of these NPCs was to add them to your party. The function of the rest is impossible to know.\par
   One door (Index 10) leads to this map. This door is actually assigned to a map trigger on Map ID: 81 (Potos Fields 2).\par
   The trigger is located out of bounds on the west side of the map between the bushes on the other side of the exit leading to the Potos Waterfall Base.\par
